  "id": "inner-speech",
  "term": "inner speech",
  "definition": "Inner speech is speech imagined in the mind without speaking out loud. In this context, it is discussed as a signal that brain-computer systems may try to decode to help restore communication, raising important ethical and privacy concerns.",
